# Build artefacts this repo's own commands produce, and the one file that must never be
# committed. frontend/.gitignore already covers the TypeScript side (node_modules/, dist/,
# *.tsbuildinfo) — this is the Go side, which had nothing.
#
# ⚠ WHY IT EXISTS: `go build ./cmd/track` drops a `track` binary in the repo root, and
# during W3.47 `git add -A` STAGED IT. Caught by reading `git status` before committing;
# `git commit -a` would have put ~40 MB in main. cmd/track/gitignore_test.go keeps these
# rules real and, just as importantly, keeps them from getting broad enough to hide source.

# ⚠ LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Bare `track` would also match the DIRECTORY cmd/track —
# the entire main package. The guard's mustBeTracked list asserts cmd/track/main.go is
# still visible precisely because that mistake is one character away.
/track
/bin/

# Local environment. .env.example is the committed template and is deliberately NOT matched
# by this pattern; a real .env holds every credential .env.example documents.
.env

.DS_Store
